# Emissions MAP Expansion Plan

The "Emissions MAP" (formerly Methane Explorer) will be enhanced to display all major Sonatrach facilities with accurate coordinates, searchable emissions data, and smooth map transitions.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Backend: Data Infrastructure
- **[MODIFY] [models.py](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/new/server/models.py)**: Added `latitude` and `longitude` to the [Facility](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/new/server/models.py#32-50) model.
- **[MODIFY] [routes/facilities.py](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/new/server/routes/facilities.py)**: Updated API to return and accept coordinates.
- **[NEW] [seed_map_data.py](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/new/server/seed_map_data.py)**: Script to populate the database with Sonatrach's major field and refinery locations.

### 2. Frontend: Map & Search Logic
- **[MODIFY] [MethaneExplorer.jsx](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/h/new/client/src/pages/MethaneExplorer.jsx)**:
    - Renamed internal references to "Emissions MAP".
    - Removed "LIVE" tags.
    - Updated to fetch facility list from `/api/facilities` and use backend coordinates.
    - Enhanced search to filter by name and check if emissions data exists.
    - Improved selection logic to "fly to" coordinates of any facility, even those without current data (showing a placeholder for them).

## Verification Plan
1. Run `seed_map_data.py` to populate DB.
2. Open Emissions MAP and verify all major markers (Hassi Messaoud, Arzew, etc.) are visible.
3. Search for a facility and click to verify the fly-to animation.
4. Verify "LIVE" tags are gone.
